{
  "source": "Prompts/embrace-the-future-opener-v8.mp4",
  "duration": 145.6853125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.2,
      "text": "Up to this point, you've learned exactly how to use AI in your daily life."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.74,
      "end": 7.18,
      "text": "You understand the underlying engine running it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.42,
      "end": 9.4,
      "text": "which means that when the model behaves strangely,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.12,
      "end": 12.84,
      "text": "that strange behavior actually makes perfect sense to you."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.24,
      "end": 16.5,
      "text": "Your initial goal for this course was to be smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.0,
      "end": 18.04,
      "text": "Consider that done."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.8,
      "end": 20.94,
      "text": "But understanding how a tool works mechanically"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.94,
      "end": 24.92,
      "text": "doesn't automatically tell us how it will impact society in the long run."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.32,
      "end": 28.68,
      "text": "There's the optimist, who thinks AI is completely fantastic."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.68,
      "end": 32.08,
      "text": "There's the warrior, who was convinced it will hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.88,
      "end": 35.2,
      "text": "Here's the honest part, nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.06,
      "end": 39.58,
      "text": "Not them, not us, not the people building AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.36,
      "end": 44.22,
      "text": "Centuries ago, map makers had to chart vast expanses of ocean"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.22,
      "end": 46.3,
      "text": "they simply did not understand yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.94,
      "end": 48.88,
      "text": "Whenever they reached the edges of their knowledge,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.32,
      "end": 53.72,
      "text": "they would fill the blank waters with imaginary sea monsters and strange serpents."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.38,
      "end": 58.2,
      "text": "The future of AI is like the unknown parts of the ocean on those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.2,
      "end": 61.56,
      "text": "Warriors fill the unknown parts with AI monsters"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.56,
      "end": 65.18,
      "text": "that destroy jobs, hack systems, and take over the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.84,
      "end": 68.26,
      "text": "AI optimists look at the same unknown parts"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.26,
      "end": 71.26,
      "text": "and see easy, clear sailing through open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.94,
      "end": 75.98,
      "text": "History shows us that early sailors never actually encountered literal sea monsters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.68,
      "end": 79.08,
      "text": "but they also rarely got easy, clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.82,
      "end": 82.56,
      "text": "Instead, they usually found something entirely unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.38,
      "end": 87.62,
      "text": "So as we move forward, we are going to take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.62,
      "end": 91.76,
      "text": "We will look at the monsters, and we will look at the open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.46,
      "end": 95.48,
      "text": "Right now, there is only one absolute certainty."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.06,
      "end": 97.62,
      "text": "AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.28,
      "end": 102.6,
      "text": "That doesn't mean it will keep getting better forever, just that it isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.28,
      "end": 107.4,
      "text": "This roadmap shows what will explore in this section, embrace the future."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.14,
      "end": 111.98,
      "text": "One, the argument, the loudest voices, why they disagree,"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.5,
      "end": 114.8,
      "text": "and why the speed makes the argument louder."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.8,
      "end": 120.02,
      "text": "Two, monsters and open water, the honest case for worry"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.02,
      "end": 123.4,
      "text": "alongside the real world upside that has already happened."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.22,
      "end": 129.34,
      "text": "Three, where it lands on you, how AI acts, how work may change,"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.88,
      "end": 133.4,
      "text": "the bill for all that math, and what history teaches about predictions."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.6,
      "end": 136.3,
      "text": "Take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 137.22,
      "end": 138.78,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.36,
      "end": 141.2,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    }
  ],
